-- runtime filters disabled: the probe read as it is, the merge join reads the hundredth of it that the build side covers
merge join
-- the probe filtered on another column: its keys stay spread over its range, assuming independent columns
merge join
-- the same with optimize_move_to_prewhere
merge join
-- the same written as PREWHERE
merge join
-- the probe filtered on its key: its keys need not be spread over its range, the merge is charged the whole probe
hash join
-- the same with optimize_move_to_prewhere
hash join
-- the same written as PREWHERE
hash join
-- a read limit that stops the read instead of failing the query: it may drop rows of any column, the merge is charged the whole probe
hash join
-- the build side filtered on its key: its keys still lie in its range, the merge reads that hundredth
merge join
-- with the runtime filter: the probe read as it is, a hash join reads a tenth of it
hash joins only
-- the probe filtered on another column: a hash join reads a tenth of it
hash joins only
-- the probe filtered on its key: the hash join is charged the whole probe, which is merge-joined with the sorted build side
uses a merge join
-- the build side filtered on its key: it still bounds the probe, a hash join reads a tenth of it
hash joins only
-- a build side over the same tenth read with FINAL, which may rewrite values: it does not bound the probe, which is merge-joined
uses a merge join
-- a build side with measured statistics, runtime filters disabled: the merge join reads the few probe keys it covers
merge join
-- statistics that miss a part: the range need not enclose the keys, the merge is charged the whole probe
hash join
